For understanding the situation, the most important factors are that no one’s authority should be beyond challenge—since equal standing prohibits unchallengeable hierarchies—and that fairness outweighs tradition. Traditional authority claiming earned wisdom holds little moral weight in this framework because it risks undermining equal voice and accountability.

